settings.sisyphus:compatibility=Compatibility
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_moss=Moss
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_moss.tooltip=Master toggle for the moss block and moss carpet. When disabled, they are not registered and their recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_stripped_wood=Stripped Logs and Wood
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_stripped_wood.tooltip=Master toggle for wood, stripped logs and stripped wood, including stripping with an axe. When disabled, the blocks are not registered and their recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.strippable_blocks=Strippable Blocks
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.strippable_blocks.tooltip=Extra blocks that can be stripped with an axe, for modded woods, in the format 'modid:log=modid:stripped_log'. The rotation of the log is kept. Blocks named 'stripped_<name>' next to a block called '<name>' are found automatically.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_prismarine_stairs_and_slabs=Prismarine Stairs and Slabs
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_prismarine_stairs_and_slabs.tooltip=Master toggle for prismarine, prismarine brick and dark prismarine stairs and slabs. When disabled, they are not registered and their recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_smooth_blocks=Smooth Blocks
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_smooth_blocks.tooltip=Master toggle for the smooth stone, smooth sandstone, smooth red sandstone and smooth quartz blocks. When disabled, they are not registered and their smelting recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_stone_variants=Stone Stairs, Slabs and Walls
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_stone_variants.tooltip=Master toggle for the stairs, slabs and walls of stone, andesite, diorite, granite, mossy blocks, red nether brick, end stone brick and the other stone types added in 1.14. When disabled, they are not registered and their recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_blackstone=Blackstone
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_blackstone.tooltip=Master toggle for blackstone and its polished, chiseled and brick variants, with their stairs, slabs, walls, buttons and pressure plates. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_basalt=Basalt
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_basalt.tooltip=Master toggle for basalt and polished basalt. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_nether_brick_variants=Nether Brick Variants
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_nether_brick_variants.tooltip=Master toggle for chiseled nether bricks, cracked nether bricks and quartz bricks. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_crying_obsidian=Crying Obsidian
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_crying_obsidian.tooltip=Master toggle for crying obsidian. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_soul_soil=Soul Soil
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_soul_soil.tooltip=Master toggle for soul soil. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_shroomlight=Shroomlight
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_shroomlight.tooltip=Master toggle for the shroomlight. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_nether_gold=Nether Gold Ore
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_nether_gold.tooltip=Master toggle for nether gold ore. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_nether_wood=Nether Wood
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_nether_wood.tooltip=Master toggle for the crimson and warped wood: stems, hyphae, planks, slabs, stairs, fences, gates, buttons, pressure plates, doors, trapdoors and signs. Huge fungi need it. When disabled, they are not registered and their recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_cherry_wood=Cherry Wood
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_cherry_wood.tooltip=Master toggle for the cherry wood: logs, wood, stripped logs and wood, planks, slabs, stairs, fences, gates, buttons, pressure plates, doors, trapdoors, the sign and the bookshelf. The cherry trees under Plants need it. When disabled, they are not registered and their recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_bamboo_wood=Bamboo Wood
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_bamboo_wood.tooltip=Master toggle for the bamboo wood: blocks of bamboo and of stripped bamboo, planks, bamboo mosaic, slabs, stairs, fences, gates, buttons, pressure plates, doors, trapdoors, the sign, the bookshelf, the raft and the chest raft. A block of bamboo is crafted from nine bamboo, so it needs Bamboo in Plants. When disabled, they are not registered and their recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_hanging_signs=Hanging Signs
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_hanging_signs.tooltip=Master toggle for the hanging signs of 1.20, of oak, spruce, birch, jungle, acacia and dark oak, and of crimson, warped, cherry and bamboo when their wood is on. Each is crafted from two chains and six stripped logs of its wood (stripped blocks of bamboo for bamboo), so it needs the chain and the stripped logs too. When disabled, they are not registered and their recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_signs=New Signs
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_signs.tooltip=Master toggle for the spruce, birch, jungle, acacia and dark oak signs, and dyeing sign text. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_modded_wood_signs=Signs of Modded Woods
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_modded_wood_signs.tooltip=Makes a sign for each wood of another mod that has none: a mod with a <wood>_log and a <wood>_planks block and no sign of that wood gets one, crafted from six of the planks over a stick, which sounds like the planks. Its pictures are made when the game loads, from those of the oak sign in the colours of the planks. It needs the new signs to be on.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.detect_modded_woods=Detect Modded Woods Automatically
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.detect_modded_woods.tooltip=Finds the woods of other mods that get a sign by the names of their blocks: a <wood>_log and a <wood>_planks block of the same mod, and no sign of that wood. When disabled, only the woods in Modded Sign Woods get one.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.modded_sign_woods=Modded Sign Woods
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.modded_sign_woods.tooltip=Woods of other mods that get a sign although their blocks are not named <wood>_log and <wood>_planks, in the format 'modid:log=modid:planks'. Add '@meta' after the planks when they are one kind of a block, and '=name' at the end to name the sign sisyphus:<modid>_<name>_sign; otherwise the name is made from those of the planks or the log and the meta. Example: 'examplemod:log_fir=examplemod:planks@2=fir'.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_wood_bookshelves=Wood Bookshelves
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_wood_bookshelves.tooltip=Master toggle for the bookshelves of spruce, birch, jungle, acacia and dark oak, and of crimson and warped when the nether wood is on, as other mods have them. Each is crafted like the oak bookshelf from the planks of its wood, so the oak bookshelf then needs oak planks. When disabled, they are not registered and their recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_chain=Chain
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_chain.tooltip=Master toggle for the chain. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_lantern=Lantern
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_lantern.tooltip=Master toggle for the lantern. When disabled, they are not registered and their recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_candles=Candles
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_candles.tooltip=Master toggle for candles of the 17 colors and the cakes with a candle on them. When disabled, they are not registered and their recipes are removed. A candle is made of string and honeycomb from another mod, or of string and a slime ball.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_amethyst=Amethyst
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_amethyst.tooltip=Master toggle for amethyst: the block, budding amethyst, the buds and clusters that grow on it, the shard, tinted glass, calcite and smooth basalt. When disabled, they are not registered and their recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_mud=Mud
settings.sisyphus:building_blocks.enable_mud.tooltip=Master toggle for mud, packed mud and mud bricks of 1.19, with the stairs, slab and wall of mud bricks, and making mud with a water bottle on dirt. The trail ruins are built of mud bricks, and are built of bricks when it is off.
settings.sisyphus:deepslate.enable_deepslate=Deepslate
settings.sisyphus:deepslate.enable_deepslate.tooltip=Master toggle for all deepslate content. When disabled, no deepslate blocks, items, recipes or ore dictionary entries are registered and deepslate world generation is skipped.
settings.sisyphus:deepslate.enable_deepslate_generation=Deepslate Generation
settings.sisyphus:deepslate.deepslate_y_threshold=Y-Level Threshold
settings.sisyphus:deepslate.deepslate_y_threshold.tooltip=The Y-level at which deepslate generation starts. Blocks below this level will be replaced with deepslate variants.
settings.sisyphus:deepslate.deepslate_transition_range=Transition Range
settings.sisyphus:deepslate.deepslate_transition_range.tooltip=The range (in blocks) over which deepslate gradually replaces stone around the Y-threshold. 0 = instant transition, higher values = more gradual.
settings.sisyphus:deepslate.deepslate_dimensions=Dimensions
settings.sisyphus:deepslate.deepslate_dimensions.tooltip=The dimensions, by number, that stone is turned to deepslate in: 0 is the Overworld, -1 the Nether and 1 the End. Leave it empty for every dimension.
settings.sisyphus:deepslate.replace_ores_with_deepslate=Replace Ores in Deepslate
settings.sisyphus:deepslate.enable_deepslate_mod_ores=Modded Deepslate Ores
settings.sisyphus:deepslate.enable_deepslate_mod_ores.tooltip=Makes a deepslate version of each ore of another mod that has a stone background: a block of rock with a single state and no tile entity, called an ore or in the ore dictionary as one. Where its picture shows the stone of the game, deepslate is drawn instead. It needs deepslate to be on, and drops, experience and smelting are those of the ore.
settings.sisyphus:deepslate.deepslate_ore_whitelist=Ore Whitelist
settings.sisyphus:deepslate.deepslate_ore_whitelist.tooltip=Ores that get a deepslate version whatever their name is, as 'modid:block' or 'modid:*', if they are simple blocks of rock.
settings.sisyphus:deepslate.deepslate_ore_blacklist=Ore Blacklist
settings.sisyphus:deepslate.deepslate_ore_blacklist.tooltip=Ores that do not get a deepslate version, as 'modid:block' or 'modid:*'.
settings.sisyphus:plants.enable_flowers=Flowers and Dyes
settings.sisyphus:plants.enable_flowers.tooltip=Master toggle for the cornflower, lily of the valley and wither rose, and the blue, white, black and brown dyes. When disabled, they are not registered and their recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:plants.enable_sweet_berries=Sweet Berries
settings.sisyphus:plants.enable_sweet_berries.tooltip=Master toggle for sweet berries and sweet berry bushes. When disabled, they are not registered and their recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:plants.enable_bamboo=Bamboo
settings.sisyphus:plants.enable_bamboo.tooltip=Master toggle for bamboo and bamboo shoots, including the sticks that can be crafted from it. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:plants.enable_nether_fungi=Nether Fungi
settings.sisyphus:plants.enable_nether_fungi.tooltip=Master toggle for the crimson and warped plants: the two nylium blocks, fungi, roots, nether sprouts, weeping and twisting vines and the warped wart block. Where they grow in the Nether is under World Generation. When disabled, they are not registered.
settings.sisyphus:plants.enable_lush_plants=Lush Cave Plants
settings.sisyphus:plants.enable_lush_plants.tooltip=Master toggle for the plants of the lush caves: azalea and its leaves, glow lichen, spore blossom, hanging roots and rooted dirt. When disabled, they are not registered.
settings.sisyphus:plants.enable_cherry_trees=Cherry Trees
settings.sisyphus:plants.enable_cherry_trees.tooltip=Master toggle for the cherry trees: cherry leaves, which shed pink petals, the cherry sapling and pink petals. Needs Cherry Wood in Building Blocks. Where they grow is under World Generation. When disabled, they are not registered and their recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:plants.enable_cave_vines=Cave Vines
settings.sisyphus:plants.enable_cave_vines.tooltip=Master toggle for cave vines and the glow berries that grow on them. When disabled, they are not registered.
settings.sisyphus:plants.enable_dripleaf=Dripleaf
settings.sisyphus:plants.enable_dripleaf.tooltip=Master toggle for the big and small dripleaf. When disabled, they are not registered.
settings.sisyphus:plants.pot_any_small_plant=Pot Any Small Plant
settings.sisyphus:plants.pot_any_small_plant.tooltip=Let flower pots hold the small plants of other mods and of this mod, besides those of the game: any plant that grows on the ground and is one block tall, such as a flower, a sapling, a mushroom, a fungus or roots, and the Extra Potted Plants. It is drawn at three quarters of its size, like the plants of the game in a pot. Needs MixinBooter or FermiumBooter.
settings.sisyphus:plants.extra_potted_plants=Extra Potted Plants
settings.sisyphus:plants.extra_potted_plants.tooltip=More plants that flower pots hold with Pot Any Small Plant, as 'modid:block' or 'modid:*': plants that do not grow like a flower, such as the azaleas.
settings.sisyphus:plants.unpottable_plants=Unpottable Plants
settings.sisyphus:plants.unpottable_plants.tooltip=Plants that flower pots do not hold with Pot Any Small Plant, as 'modid:block' or 'modid:*', for plants that look wrong in a pot. The plants of the game that fit in a pot always do.
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_composter=Composter
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_composter.tooltip=Master toggle for the composter. When disabled, they are not registered and their recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_barrel=Barrel
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_barrel.tooltip=Master toggle for the barrel. When disabled, they are not registered and their recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_workstations=Fletching and Smithing Tables
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_workstations.tooltip=Master toggle for the fletching table and the smithing table. When disabled, they are not registered and their recipes are removed. The fletching table is a decorative block, as it is in the game; when the Fletchery mod is installed, its fletching table, which has a screen, is used in place of this one.
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_furnaces=Blast Furnace and Smoker
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_furnaces.tooltip=Master toggle for the blast furnace and the smoker. When disabled, they are not registered and their recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_grindstone=Grindstone
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_grindstone.tooltip=Master toggle for the grindstone. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_stonecutter=Stonecutter
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_stonecutter.tooltip=Master toggle for the stonecutter. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_loom=Loom
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_loom.tooltip=Master toggle for the loom and banner patterns. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_cartography_table=Cartography Table
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_cartography_table.tooltip=Master toggle for the cartography table. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_lectern=Lectern
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_lectern.tooltip=Master toggle for the lectern. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.lectern_holds_maps=Lectern Holds Maps
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.lectern_holds_maps.tooltip=Lets a filled map be put on the lectern instead of a book. It is drawn on the top of the lectern, and using the lectern shows it big.
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.lectern_items=Lectern Items
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.lectern_items.tooltip=Other items that can be put on the lectern, as registry names where * stands for anything: 'modid:item', 'modid:*' or '*book*'. Using the lectern then uses the item, as if it were held, which opens the screen of a guide book. Blocks are left out.
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_bell=Bell
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_bell.tooltip=Master toggle for the bell. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.bell_sends_villagers_indoors=Bell Sends Villagers Indoors
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.bell_sends_villagers_indoors.tooltip=Ringing a bell sends the villagers within 32 blocks of it into the houses of their village, as in 1.14. Each one runs to the nearest house that is not yet crowded and stays inside for 15 seconds; one with no house within 32 blocks stays where it is.
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_scaffolding=Scaffolding
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_scaffolding.tooltip=Master toggle for scaffolding. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_campfire=Campfire
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_campfire.tooltip=Master toggle for the campfire. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_soul_fire=Soul Fire
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_soul_fire.tooltip=Master toggle for soul fire, the soul torch, the soul lantern and the soul campfire. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_respawn_anchor=Respawn Anchor
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_respawn_anchor.tooltip=Master toggle for the respawn anchor. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_lodestone=Lodestone
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_lodestone.tooltip=Master toggle for the lodestone and the lodestone compass. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_target=Target Block
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_target.tooltip=Master toggle for the target block. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_note_block_sounds=New Note Block Sounds
settings.sisyphus:functional_blocks.enable_note_block_sounds.tooltip=Master toggle for the six new note block instruments. When disabled, they are not registered and their recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:crossbow=Crossbow
settings.sisyphus:crossbow.enabled=Enabled
settings.sisyphus:crossbow.enabled.tooltip=Master toggle for the crossbow. When disabled, it and its enchantments are not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:crossbow.durability=Durability
settings.sisyphus:crossbow.durability.tooltip=How many times the crossbow can be used before it breaks. 1.18 has 465, and 1.14 had 326.
settings.sisyphus:crossbow.reload_time=Reload Time
settings.sisyphus:crossbow.reload_time.tooltip=How many ticks it takes to load the crossbow. 20 ticks are a second. Each level of Quick Charge takes a fifth of it off, so Quick Charge III loads in 10 of the 25.
settings.sisyphus:crossbow.damage_multiplier=Damage Multiplier
settings.sisyphus:crossbow.damage_multiplier.tooltip=How much harder than an arrow from a bow an arrow from the crossbow hits, as a multiple of the damage of the arrow. At 1, a plain arrow hits for 7 to 11 points, as in 1.14. Firework rockets are not changed.
settings.sisyphus:crossbow.enable_multishot=Multishot
settings.sisyphus:crossbow.enable_multishot.tooltip=Toggle for the Multishot enchantment, which loads three arrows or rockets at once. When disabled, it is not registered.
settings.sisyphus:crossbow.enable_quick_charge=Quick Charge
settings.sisyphus:crossbow.enable_quick_charge.tooltip=Toggle for the Quick Charge enchantment, which loads the crossbow faster. When disabled, it is not registered.
settings.sisyphus:crossbow.enable_piercing=Piercing
settings.sisyphus:crossbow.enable_piercing.tooltip=Toggle for the Piercing enchantment, which lets arrows fly through mobs. When disabled, it is not registered.
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs=Throwing Discs
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.enabled=Enabled
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.enabled.tooltip=Master toggle for the throwing discs of gold, iron and diamond, and of netherite when netherite is on. A thrown disc flies straight, cuts through mobs, bounces off hard blocks and comes back to the thrower. When disabled, they are not registered and their recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.damage=Damage
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.damage.tooltip=How much harder than the attack damage of its material a disc hits each mob. A sword adds 4, so 3 makes a disc one point weaker than a sword of the same material: 4 for gold, 5 for iron, 6 for diamond and 7 for netherite.
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.speed=Speed
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.speed.tooltip=How fast a disc flies when it is thrown, in blocks per tick. Each level of Velocity adds 20 percent. Bounces make it faster, up to 2.4 or this speed, if that is more.
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.range=Range
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.range.tooltip=How many blocks a disc flies out before it turns back. Each level of Reach adds 2, and each bounce 5.
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.bounces=Bounces
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.bounces.tooltip=At which bounce off a block a disc turns back. Each level of Ricochet adds 2. 1 sends it back from the first block it hits.
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.bounce_wear=Bounce Wear
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.bounce_wear.tooltip=The durability that each bounce costs. Each throw and each mob hit cost one. Unbreaking can save some of it.
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.cooldown=Cooldown
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.cooldown.tooltip=How many ticks a player waits after a throw before they can throw a disc again. 20 ticks are a second.
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.wind_up=Wind-up
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.wind_up.tooltip=How many ticks a player holds use to draw a disc back before it can be thrown, as with a bow: it is thrown when use is let go, and letting go sooner throws nothing. 20 ticks are a second. 0 throws it at once, without drawing it back. On a server, the server's value counts.
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.enable_velocity=Velocity
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.enable_velocity.tooltip=Toggle for the Velocity enchantment, which makes a disc fly faster. When disabled, it is not registered.
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.enable_ricochet=Ricochet
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.enable_ricochet.tooltip=Toggle for the Ricochet enchantment, which lets a disc bounce more often and speeds up its bounces. When disabled, it is not registered.
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.enable_reach=Reach
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.enable_reach.tooltip=Toggle for the Reach enchantment, which lets a disc fly further before it turns back. When disabled, it is not registered.
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.enable_rebound=Rebound
settings.sisyphus:throwing_discs.enable_rebound.tooltip=Toggle for the Rebound enchantment, which lets a disc on its way back hurt the mobs it already hit. When disabled, it is not registered.
settings.sisyphus:items.enable_netherite=Netherite
settings.sisyphus:items.enable_netherite.tooltip=Master toggle for netherite: ancient debris, scrap, ingots, blocks, tools and armor, and upgrading diamond gear in the smithing table. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:items.netherite_needs_template=Netherite Upgrade Needs Template
settings.sisyphus:items.netherite_needs_template.tooltip=Upgrading diamond gear to netherite in the smithing table needs a netherite upgrade smithing template, as in 1.20. The template is found in the chests of nether fortresses, in place of the bastion remnants, and copied with diamonds and netherrack. When disabled, the netherite ingot alone upgrades it, as in 1.16, and the template is not found in chests.
settings.sisyphus:items.enable_armor_trims=Armor Trims
settings.sisyphus:items.enable_armor_trims.tooltip=Master toggle for the armor trims: the armor trim smithing templates, which are found in structures and give armor a pattern in the smithing table, in the color of the ingot or crystal it is made with. Needs the smithing table (Enable Fletching and Smithing Tables). When disabled, the templates are not registered and their recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:items.enable_leather_horse_armor=Leather Horse Armor
settings.sisyphus:items.enable_leather_horse_armor.tooltip=Master toggle for leather horse armor. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:items.enable_suspicious_stew=Suspicious Stew
settings.sisyphus:items.enable_suspicious_stew.tooltip=Master toggle for suspicious stew. When disabled, they are not registered and their recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:items.enable_slow_falling=Slow Falling
settings.sisyphus:items.enable_slow_falling.tooltip=Master toggle for the Slow Falling effect and the potions and tipped arrows that use it. When disabled, none of it is registered.
settings.sisyphus:items.enable_soul_speed=Soul Speed
settings.sisyphus:items.enable_soul_speed.tooltip=Master toggle for the Soul Speed enchantment. When disabled, it is not registered.
settings.sisyphus:items.enable_snout_pattern=Snout Banner Pattern
settings.sisyphus:items.enable_snout_pattern.tooltip=Master toggle for the Snout banner pattern and its banner pattern item. It also needs the loom. When disabled, it is not registered.
settings.sisyphus:items.enable_pigstep=Pigstep
settings.sisyphus:items.enable_pigstep.tooltip=Master toggle for the Pigstep music disc. When disabled, it is not registered.
settings.sisyphus:items.enable_otherside=Otherside
settings.sisyphus:items.enable_otherside.tooltip=Master toggle for the Otherside music disc, by Lena Raine, which is found in the chests of stronghold corridors and now and then in those of monster rooms, as in 1.18. When disabled, it is not registered.
settings.sisyphus:archaeology.enable_archaeology=Archaeology
settings.sisyphus:archaeology.enable_archaeology.tooltip=Master toggle for the archaeology of 1.20: the brush, suspicious sand and suspicious gravel, the pottery sherds and the decorated pot. When disabled, none of it is registered and its recipes and advancements are removed.
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_fish=Fish
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_fish.tooltip=Master toggle for cod, salmon, pufferfish and tropical fish. When disabled, the fish are not registered, so they do not spawn and have no spawn eggs.
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_cats=Cats
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_cats.tooltip=Master toggle for the cat and the cat spawn egg. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_foxes=Foxes
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_foxes.tooltip=Master toggle for the fox and the fox spawn egg. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_pandas=Pandas
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_pandas.tooltip=Master toggle for the panda and the panda spawn egg. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_brown_mooshroom=Brown Mooshroom
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_brown_mooshroom.tooltip=Master toggle for the brown mooshroom and milking mooshrooms for suspicious stew. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_goats=Goats
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_goats.tooltip=Master toggle for the goat of 1.17 and the goat spawn egg. When disabled, it is not registered and its advancement is removed.
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_goat_horns=Goat Horns
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_goat_horns.tooltip=Master toggle for the goat horn of 1.19, which a goat drops when it rams a log, stone, packed ice or a coal, iron or emerald ore instead of what it aimed at. Each goat has two horns, which play one of eight calls; screaming goats have calls of their own. Needs the goats. When disabled, goats keep their horns.
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_axolotls=Axolotls
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_axolotls.tooltip=Master toggle for the axolotl of 1.17, the bucket of axolotl and the axolotl spawn egg. When disabled, they are not registered and their advancements are removed.
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_wandering_trader=Wandering Trader
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_wandering_trader.tooltip=Master toggle for the wandering trader and his trader llamas, including their spawning and spawn eggs. When disabled, they are not registered.
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_piglins=Piglins
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_piglins.tooltip=Master toggle for the piglin: bartering, hunting and turning into zombified piglins, which are drawn with their new model. When disabled, it is not registered and does not spawn.
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_hoglins=Hoglins
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_hoglins.tooltip=Master toggle for the hoglin and the zoglin. When disabled, they are not registered and do not spawn, and piglins have nothing to hunt.
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_striders=Striders
settings.sisyphus:mobs.enable_striders.tooltip=Master toggle for the strider and the warped fungus on a stick. When disabled, they are not registered and do not spawn, and their recipe is removed.
settings.sisyphus:biomes.enable_bamboo_jungle=Bamboo Jungle
settings.sisyphus:biomes.enable_bamboo_jungle.tooltip=Master toggle for the bamboo jungle biome. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:biomes.bamboo_jungle_weight=Bamboo Jungle Weight
settings.sisyphus:biomes.bamboo_jungle_weight.tooltip=How often the bamboo jungle is picked among the warm biomes. A jungle has 10 and a desert 30.
settings.sisyphus:biomes.enable_cherry_grove=Cherry Grove
settings.sisyphus:biomes.enable_cherry_grove.tooltip=Master toggle for the cherry grove biome: hills of pale green grass under cherry trees, with pink petals on the ground. Needs Cherry Trees in Plants. When disabled, it is not registered.
settings.sisyphus:biomes.cherry_grove_weight=Cherry Grove Weight
settings.sisyphus:biomes.cherry_grove_weight.tooltip=How often the cherry grove is picked among the cool biomes. A forest, the extreme hills, a taiga and the plains have 10 each.
settings.sisyphus:world_generation.enable_village_workstations=Workstations in Villages
settings.sisyphus:world_generation.enable_village_workstations.tooltip=Put the workstations of 1.14 in the villages, in new chunks: the lectern and the cartography table in the library, the blast furnace, smithing table and grindstone at the blacksmith, the smoker at the butcher, the loom and the barrel in the big house, the fletching table and the stonecutter in the small huts, a composter at each field and a bell under the roof of the well. Each one needs its block to be turned on.
settings.sisyphus:world_generation.enable_desert_archaeology=Suspicious Sand in Deserts
settings.sisyphus:world_generation.enable_desert_archaeology.tooltip=Generate suspicious sand in desert pyramids and desert wells, as in 1.20: a hidden room of sand under each pyramid, and two blocks under the water of each well. Only in new chunks, and only with Archaeology on.
settings.sisyphus:trail_ruins.enabled=Enabled
settings.sisyphus:trail_ruins.enabled.tooltip=Generate the trail ruins of 1.20 in new chunks: buried towers, halls, houses and roads in taigas, birch forests and jungles, with suspicious gravel that holds pottery sherds. Only with Archaeology on.
settings.sisyphus:trail_ruins.spacing=Spacing
settings.sisyphus:trail_ruins.spacing.tooltip=How far apart the trail ruins are: the world is cut into squares of this many chunks, and each square can have one, if its place is in a taiga, a birch forest or a jungle. Only places that are not planned yet change.
settings.sisyphus:trail_ruins.separation=Separation
settings.sisyphus:trail_ruins.separation.tooltip=How many chunks apart two trail ruins are at least. It is kept below the spacing.
settings.sisyphus:trail_ruins.dimensions=Dimensions
settings.sisyphus:trail_ruins.dimensions.tooltip=The dimensions, by number, that trail ruins are made in: 0 is the Overworld, -1 the Nether and 1 the End. Leave it empty for every dimension. They are never made in flat worlds or with structures turned off.
settings.sisyphus:ocean_ruins.enabled=Enabled
settings.sisyphus:ocean_ruins.enabled.tooltip=Generate the ocean ruins of 1.13 in new chunks: ruins of stone bricks or sandstone on the floor of the oceans, with chests and with suspicious gravel or sand that holds pottery sherds. Whether a ruin is cold or warm depends on the region, as 1.12 has only one kind of ocean. Only with Archaeology on.
settings.sisyphus:ocean_ruins.spacing=Spacing
settings.sisyphus:ocean_ruins.spacing.tooltip=How far apart the ocean ruins are: the world is cut into squares of this many chunks, and each square can have one, if its place is in an ocean. Only places that are not planned yet change.
settings.sisyphus:ocean_ruins.separation=Separation
settings.sisyphus:ocean_ruins.separation.tooltip=How many chunks apart two ocean ruins are at least. It is kept below the spacing.
settings.sisyphus:ocean_ruins.dimensions=Dimensions
settings.sisyphus:ocean_ruins.dimensions.tooltip=The dimensions, by number, that ocean ruins are made in: 0 is the Overworld, -1 the Nether and 1 the End. Leave it empty for every dimension. They are never made in flat worlds or with structures turned off.
settings.sisyphus:abandoned_camps.enabled=Enabled
settings.sisyphus:abandoned_camps.enabled.tooltip=Make abandoned camps in new chunks, from Wilderlands: a white tent with one slope fallen in, on birch poles and hung with cobwebs, in a worn clearing with a chest of the campers' supplies, a bench and a bedroll, on flat grassy ground in plains, savannas, forests and taigas.
settings.sisyphus:abandoned_camps.spacing=Spacing
settings.sisyphus:abandoned_camps.spacing.tooltip=How far apart the camps are: the world is cut into squares of this many chunks, and each square can have one, where it has flat ground in a fitting biome.
settings.sisyphus:abandoned_camps.chance=Chance
settings.sisyphus:abandoned_camps.chance.tooltip=How many of the squares get a camp where they have room for one, in percent.
settings.sisyphus:abandoned_camps.max_relief=Steepest Ground
settings.sisyphus:abandoned_camps.max_relief.tooltip=How much higher the highest ground under the clearing of a camp may be than the lowest, in blocks.
settings.sisyphus:abandoned_camps.min_spawn_distance=Distance From Spawn
settings.sisyphus:abandoned_camps.min_spawn_distance.tooltip=How close to the world spawn a camp may be, in blocks: none is made nearer than this.
settings.sisyphus:abandoned_camps.dimensions=Dimensions
settings.sisyphus:abandoned_camps.dimensions.tooltip=The dimensions, by number, that camps are made in: 0 is the Overworld, -1 the Nether and 1 the End. Leave it empty for every dimension. They are never made in flat worlds or with structures turned off.
settings.sisyphus:ruined_portals.enabled=Enabled
settings.sisyphus:ruined_portals.enabled.tooltip=Generate the ruined portals of 1.16 in new chunks: broken frames of obsidian and crying obsidian on a patch of netherrack, with a chest of gold. They lie on the ground, half buried in deserts, overgrown in jungles, sunk in oceans and swamps, deep in mountains or under the ground, and of blackstone in the Nether. Turned off when Unseen's Nether Backport is installed, which has them too, unless Yield to Unseen's Nether Backport is off.
settings.sisyphus:ruined_portals.spacing=Spacing
settings.sisyphus:ruined_portals.spacing.tooltip=How far apart the ruined portals are: the world is cut into squares of this many chunks, and each square can have one. Only places that are not planned yet change.
settings.sisyphus:ruined_portals.separation=Separation
settings.sisyphus:ruined_portals.separation.tooltip=How many chunks apart two ruined portals are at least. It is kept below the spacing.
settings.sisyphus:ruined_portals.dimensions=Dimensions
settings.sisyphus:ruined_portals.dimensions.tooltip=The dimensions, by number, that ruined portals are made in: 0 is the Overworld, -1 the Nether and 1 the End. Leave it empty for every dimension. In a dimension of Nether biomes they are of blackstone; there are none in the End. They are never made in flat worlds or with structures turned off.
settings.sisyphus:geodes.enabled=Enabled
settings.sisyphus:geodes.enabled.tooltip=Generate amethyst geodes underground in the Overworld, in new chunks. Needs Amethyst in Building Blocks.
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.enabled=Enabled
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.enabled.tooltip=Generate lush caves in the Overworld, in new chunks: zones about a hundred blocks across, about one part in fourteen of the world, with big open caves carved in them, which are covered in moss, cave vines, spore blossoms, azaleas, pools and dripleaves, with rooted azalea trees. They are zones of the caves that are there, and not biomes. Each part is only there when its content is turned on.
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.zone_coverage=Zone Coverage
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.zone_coverage.tooltip=How much of the Overworld is in lush zones, in percent. 0 makes none, 100 makes all of it lush.
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.zone_size=Zone Size
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.zone_size.tooltip=How big the lush zones are: 1 is about a hundred blocks across, 2 twice as wide. They cover as much of the world as before, so bigger zones are fewer.
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.min_height=Lowest Height
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.min_height.tooltip=The lowest height of the caves that are covered in moss, vines and the rest in a zone.
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.max_height=Highest Height
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.max_height.tooltip=The highest height of the caves that are covered in moss, vines and the rest in a zone. Only caves with rock above them are covered.
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.dimensions=Dimensions
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.dimensions.tooltip=The dimensions, by number, that lush caves are made in: 0 is the Overworld, -1 the Nether and 1 the End. Leave it empty for every dimension. The big caves are only carved in dimensions that make their caves the way the Overworld does.
settings.sisyphus:ocean_ruins.large_ruins=Large Ruins
settings.sisyphus:ocean_ruins.large_ruins.tooltip=How many of the ocean ruins are large, in percent.
settings.sisyphus:ocean_ruins.clusters=Clusters
settings.sisyphus:ocean_ruins.clusters.tooltip=How many of the large ocean ruins have small ruins around them, in percent.
settings.sisyphus:geodes.rarity=Rarity
settings.sisyphus:geodes.rarity.tooltip=One chunk in this many has a geode, on average. 1 puts one in every chunk.
settings.sisyphus:geodes.min_height=Lowest Height
settings.sisyphus:geodes.min_height.tooltip=The lowest height of the middle of a geode. A geode reaches up to seven blocks from its middle.
settings.sisyphus:geodes.max_height=Highest Height
settings.sisyphus:geodes.max_height.tooltip=The highest height of the middle of a geode.
settings.sisyphus:geodes.dimensions=Dimensions
settings.sisyphus:geodes.dimensions.tooltip=The dimensions, by number, that geodes are made in: 0 is the Overworld, -1 the Nether and 1 the End. Leave it empty for every dimension.
settings.sisyphus:wild_plants.enable_bamboo=Bamboo in Jungles
settings.sisyphus:wild_plants.enable_bamboo.tooltip=Generate thickets of bamboo in jungles. Needs Bamboo in Plants.
settings.sisyphus:wild_plants.bamboo_rarity=Bamboo Rarity
settings.sisyphus:wild_plants.bamboo_rarity.tooltip=One jungle chunk in this many has a thicket of bamboo, on average. The bamboo jungle has its own thickets.
settings.sisyphus:wild_plants.enable_sweet_berries=Sweet Berries in Taigas
settings.sisyphus:wild_plants.enable_sweet_berries.tooltip=Generate patches of sweet berry bushes in taigas. Needs Sweet Berries in Plants.
settings.sisyphus:wild_plants.sweet_berry_rarity=Sweet Berry Rarity
settings.sisyphus:wild_plants.sweet_berry_rarity.tooltip=One taiga chunk in this many has a patch of sweet berry bushes, on average.
settings.sisyphus:wild_plants.snowy_sweet_berry_rarity=Sweet Berry Rarity in Snowy Taigas
settings.sisyphus:wild_plants.snowy_sweet_berry_rarity.tooltip=One snowy taiga chunk in this many has a patch of sweet berry bushes, on average.
settings.sisyphus:wild_plants.enable_flowers=Wild Flowers
settings.sisyphus:wild_plants.enable_flowers.tooltip=Generate cornflowers in plains and lilies of the valley in forests. Needs Flowers and Dyes in Plants.
settings.sisyphus:wild_plants.cornflower_rarity=Cornflower Rarity
settings.sisyphus:wild_plants.cornflower_rarity.tooltip=One plains chunk in this many has a patch of cornflowers, on average.
settings.sisyphus:wild_plants.lily_of_the_valley_rarity=Lily of the Valley Rarity
settings.sisyphus:wild_plants.lily_of_the_valley_rarity.tooltip=One forest chunk in this many has a patch of lilies of the valley, on average.
settings.sisyphus:wild_plants.dimensions=Dimensions
settings.sisyphus:wild_plants.dimensions.tooltip=The dimensions, by number, that the wild plants grow in: 0 is the Overworld, -1 the Nether and 1 the End. Leave it empty for every dimension. They are only in biomes they belong to, jungles, taigas, plains and forests, wherever those are.
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.enable_fungi_patches=Crimson and Warped Patches
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.enable_fungi_patches.tooltip=Generate patches of crimson or warped nylium in the caves of the Nether, with roots, fungi and vines on them, and huge fungi where the nether wood is turned on. Needs Nether Fungi in Plants.
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.fungi_patch_rarity=Crimson and Warped Patch Rarity
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.fungi_patch_rarity.tooltip=One Nether chunk in this many has a crimson or warped patch, on average.
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.enable_nether_gold=Nether Gold Ore
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.enable_nether_gold.tooltip=Generate veins of nether gold ore in the netherrack. Needs Nether Gold Ore in Building Blocks.
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.nether_gold_veins=Nether Gold Ore Veins
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.nether_gold_veins.tooltip=How many veins of nether gold ore each chunk tries to make.
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.nether_gold_vein_size=Nether Gold Ore Vein Size
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.nether_gold_vein_size.tooltip=How many blocks a vein of nether gold ore has at most.
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.enable_blackstone=Blackstone
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.enable_blackstone.tooltip=Generate patches of blackstone in the netherrack. Needs Blackstone in Building Blocks.
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.blackstone_patches=Blackstone Patches
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.blackstone_patches.tooltip=How many patches of blackstone each chunk tries to make.
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.blackstone_patch_size=Blackstone Patch Size
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.blackstone_patch_size.tooltip=How many blocks a patch of blackstone has at most.
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.enable_basalt=Basalt
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.enable_basalt.tooltip=Generate patches of basalt in the netherrack. Needs Basalt in Building Blocks.
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.basalt_patches=Basalt Patches
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.basalt_patches.tooltip=How many patches of basalt each chunk tries to make.
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.basalt_patch_size=Basalt Patch Size
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.basalt_patch_size.tooltip=How many blocks a patch of basalt has at most.
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.enable_ancient_debris=Ancient Debris
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.enable_ancient_debris.tooltip=Hide ancient debris in the netherrack, where it never touches air. Needs Netherite in Items and Effects.
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.ancient_debris_tries=Ancient Debris Tries
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.ancient_debris_tries.tooltip=How many times each chunk tries to hide ancient debris. Each try hides a vein of up to three blocks low down, between heights 8 and 24, and one of up to two blocks at any height from 8 up.
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.dimensions=Dimensions
settings.sisyphus:nether_generation.dimensions.tooltip=The dimensions, by number, that the ores, stones and crimson and warped patches are put in: 0 is the Overworld, -1 the Nether and 1 the End. Leave it empty for every dimension. They only replace netherrack.
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.enable_big_caves=Big Caves
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.enable_big_caves.tooltip=Carve big open caves in the lush zones, like the caves of 1.18, as well as the narrow tunnels of 1.12. When off, the lush zones only cover the tunnels.
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.big_cave_openness=Big Cave Openness
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.big_cave_openness.tooltip=How much of the rock in the middle of a zone the big caves take, in percent, before they close off toward their floor and roof. More makes bigger halls with fewer pillars.
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.big_cave_size=Big Cave Size
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.big_cave_size.tooltip=How big the halls of the big caves are: 1 makes halls of forty to sixty blocks across and up to about thirty high, 2 twice that.
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.big_cave_min_height=Big Cave Lowest Height
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.big_cave_min_height.tooltip=The lowest height of the big caves. Below 11 the caves of 1.12 are filled with lava, so lower big caves can meet lava.
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.big_cave_max_height=Big Cave Highest Height
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.big_cave_max_height.tooltip=The highest height of the big caves.
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.big_cave_roof=Big Cave Roof
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.big_cave_roof.tooltip=How many blocks of rock are left at least between the big caves and the ground above them, or the sea floor.
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.roof_moss=Roof Moss
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.roof_moss.tooltip=How much of the roof of a lush cave is moss, in percent.
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.cave_vines=Cave Vines
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.cave_vines.tooltip=How many of the blocks of the roof have a cave vine under them, in percent.
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.glow_berries=Glow Berries
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.glow_berries.tooltip=How many of the blocks of a cave vine have glow berries, in percent.
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.longest_cave_vine=Longest Cave Vine
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.longest_cave_vine.tooltip=How long the longest cave vines are, in blocks. Most vines are one to seven blocks long, and a few are up to this long. A vine always stops a block or two above the floor.
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.spore_blossoms=Spore Blossoms
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.spore_blossoms.tooltip=How many of the blocks of the roof have a spore blossom under them, in percent.
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.glow_lichen=Glow Lichen
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.glow_lichen.tooltip=How many of the blocks of the roof have glow lichen under them, and how many of the floors have some on a wall above them, in percent.
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.floor_moss=Floor Moss
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.floor_moss.tooltip=How much of the floor of a lush cave is moss, in percent.
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.floor_plants=Floor Plants
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.floor_plants.tooltip=How much of the moss on the floor has a plant on it, in percent: grass, moss carpet, tall grass and azaleas.
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.clay_pools=Clay Pools
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.clay_pools.tooltip=How many of the floors are the middle of a pool of water on clay, in percent. A pool covers a lot of floor, so a little goes a long way.
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.largest_clay_pool=Largest Clay Pool
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.largest_clay_pool.tooltip=How far the largest pools of clay reach from their middle, in blocks. A pool reaches from two blocks less than this to this.
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.rooted_azalea_trees=Rooted Azalea Trees
settings.sisyphus:lush_caves.rooted_azalea_trees.tooltip=How many rooted azalea trees there are in each chunk of a zone, on average.
settings.sisyphus:gameplay.enable_hoe_enchanting=Enchanted and Faster Hoes
settings.sisyphus:gameplay.enable_hoe_enchanting.tooltip=Hoes can be enchanted with Efficiency, Fortune and Silk Touch (with books at an anvil, as the enchanting table only offers what has an enchantability), and mine leaves, hay bales, sponges, wart blocks, targets and shroomlights faster, as in 1.16.
settings.sisyphus:gameplay.enable_mending_repair_first=Mending Repairs First
settings.sisyphus:gameplay.enable_mending_repair_first.tooltip=Mending, as in 1.16: experience repairs every worn Mending item you carry, one after the other, before what is left fills the experience bar. When disabled, the game picks one Mending item at random and the experience goes to the bar if it needs no repair.
settings.sisyphus:gameplay.enable_enchanting_table_light=Enchanting Table Light
settings.sisyphus:gameplay.enable_enchanting_table_light.tooltip=The enchanting table gives light of level 7, as in 1.18. This needs a mixin, so it needs MixinBooter or FermiumBooter, and nothing changes without one of them. A table that is already there gives light once the light around it is worked out again, which happens when a block near it changes.
settings.sisyphus:gameplay.enable_bubble_columns=Bubble Columns
settings.sisyphus:gameplay.enable_bubble_columns.tooltip=Bubble columns, as in 1.13: water sources over soul sand push up whatever is in them, and over a magma block pull it down, a boat on top rocks and is then thrown up or pulled under, and a column gives back air. Magma blocks no longer dry up the water over them. This needs a mixin, so it needs MixinBooter or FermiumBooter, and no column is made without one of them. Water that is already over soul sand or a magma block becomes a column once a block next to it changes.
settings.sisyphus:gameplay.enable_dispenser_behaviors=Dispenser Behaviors
settings.sisyphus:gameplay.enable_dispenser_behaviors.tooltip=Dispensers, as in 1.16: put saddles on pigs, striders and tamed horses, donkeys and mules, shear sheep, mooshrooms and snow golems, and charge respawn anchors with glowstone.
settings.sisyphus:gameplay.enable_campfire_arrows=Burning Arrows Light Campfires
settings.sisyphus:gameplay.enable_campfire_arrows.tooltip=A burning arrow that hits an unlit campfire or soul campfire lights it, as in 1.16.
settings.sisyphus:gameplay.enable_soul_soil_wither=Wither on Soul Soil
settings.sisyphus:gameplay.enable_soul_soil_wither.tooltip=The wither can be built on soul soil as well as soul sand, as in 1.16. It needs soul soil to be turned on.
settings.sisyphus:gameplay.enable_endermen_nether_plants=Endermen Take Nether Plants
settings.sisyphus:gameplay.enable_endermen_nether_plants.tooltip=Endermen can pick up nylium, roots and fungi of the Nether and no longer pick up netherrack, as in 1.16.
settings.sisyphus:gameplay.enable_animals_following_food=Animals Follow Food
settings.sisyphus:gameplay.enable_animals_following_food.tooltip=Horses, donkeys and mules follow a player who holds a golden carrot, a golden apple or an enchanted golden apple, and llamas follow one who holds a hay bale, as in 1.18.
settings.sisyphus:gameplay.enable_illagers_sparing_babies=Illagers Spare Baby Villagers
settings.sisyphus:gameplay.enable_illagers_sparing_babies.tooltip=Evokers, vindicators and illusioners no longer attack baby villagers, as in 1.18.
settings.sisyphus:gameplay.enable_dark_only_spawning=Hostile Mobs Spawn Only in Darkness
settings.sisyphus:gameplay.enable_dark_only_spawning.tooltip=Hostile mobs need a light level of 0 from blocks to spawn naturally in the Overworld, as in 1.18, where they used to spawn up to level 7. A single torch keeps them away from its surroundings. It makes the game easier. Mob spawners are not changed.
settings.sisyphus:extras.enable_advancements=New Advancements
settings.sisyphus:extras.enable_advancements.tooltip=Master toggle for the advancements added in 1.14 that are not about pillagers. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:extras.enable_commands=New Commands
settings.sisyphus:extras.enable_commands.tooltip=Master toggle for the /teammsg, /schedule and /loot commands. When disabled, it is not registered and its recipes are removed.
settings.sisyphus:extras.enable_splash_texts=New Splash Texts
settings.sisyphus:extras.enable_splash_texts.tooltip=Master toggle for the new splash texts on the title screen. When disabled, only the splashes of the game are shown.
settings.sisyphus:compatibility.yield_to_unseens_nether_backport=Yield to Unseen's Nether Backport
settings.sisyphus:compatibility.yield_to_unseens_nether_backport.tooltip=When Unseen's Nether Backport is installed, turn off the content of the Nether Update that it has too, so that there are not two of each: netherite, blackstone, basalt, nether gold ore, chains, crying obsidian, soul soil, shroomlight, soul fire (with the soul torch, lantern and campfire), the respawn anchor, the lodestone, the crimson and warped plants and wood, Soul Speed, Pigstep, piglins, hoglins and striders. Your own options are not changed in the file. The target block, the snout banner pattern, the nether brick variants and the smaller changes (hoes, wither, dispensers, endermen, Mending) stay on. Set to false to keep both, with the doubles.
settings.sisyphus:compatibility.yield_to_depths_update=Yield to Depths Update
settings.sisyphus:compatibility.yield_to_depths_update.tooltip=When Depths Update is installed, turn off the content of the caves of 1.17 that it has too, so that there are not two of each and two deepslate layers in the same rock: deepslate (the blocks, their recipes, the way it is made in the world, and the deepslate versions of the ores of other mods), moss, amethyst (with calcite, smooth basalt, tinted glass and the geodes), the plants of the lush caves (with glow lichen), cave vines with glow berries, the dripleaf and lush caves. Your own options are not changed in the file. The candles and everything that is not from the caves of 1.17 stay on. If you turn one of those off in Depths Update, turn this off too, or neither mod has it. Set to false to keep both, with the doubles.
settings.sisyphus:compatibility.yield_to_quark=Yield to Quark
settings.sisyphus:compatibility.yield_to_quark.tooltip=When Quark is installed, leave the spruce, birch, jungle, acacia and dark oak bookshelves to it, so that there are not two of each with the same recipe. The crimson and warped bookshelves stay. If you turn its bookshelves off in Quark, turn this off too, or neither mod has them.
settings.sisyphus:compatibility.convert_future_mc_worlds=Convert Future MC Worlds
settings.sisyphus:compatibility.convert_future_mc_worlds.tooltip=Open worlds made with Future MC with this mod in its place: take Future MC out of the mods folder, and its blocks, items, tile entities (with their contents) and mobs become those of this mod, each chunk when it is first loaded. Content that this mod does not have (bees, honey, the trident, the scute, the nautilus shell, the globe banner pattern) stays in the save as with any removed mod; blue ice becomes packed ice, the new wooden trapdoors the oak one, and the fish buckets water buckets. Nothing is done while Future MC is installed. Back up the world first.
settings.sisyphus:compatibility.show_brushing_in_jei=Show Brushing in JEI
settings.sisyphus:compatibility.show_brushing_in_jei.tooltip=Show the Brushing tab in Just Enough Items, with everything that the suspicious sand and gravel of each place can hold and the chance of each. Turn it off to keep what is buried a surprise. On a server, the server's setting counts, and players get it when they join.
settings.sisyphus:compatibility.fletchery_integration=Fletchery Integration
settings.sisyphus:compatibility.fletchery_integration.tooltip=When Fletchery is installed, its fletching table, which has a screen, takes the place of the plain one of this mod, with the same recipe, in the recipes and in the villages. Set to false to keep the plain one.
settings.sisyphus:compatibility.oceanic_expanse_integration=Oceanic Expanse Integration
settings.sisyphus:compatibility.oceanic_expanse_integration.tooltip=When Oceanic Expanse is installed, ocean ruins get its drowned, which stay where they are put. Set to false to leave them out.

